[agent:result] The Serving Endpoints API allows you to create, update, and delete model
[agent:result]   serving endpoints.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   You can use a serving endpoint to serve models from the Databricks Model
[agent:result]   Registry or from Unity Catalog. Endpoints expose the underlying models as
[agent:result]   scalable REST API endpoints using serverless compute. This means the endpoints
[agent:result]   and associated compute resources are fully managed by Databricks and will not
[agent:result]   appear in your cloud account. A serving endpoint can consist of one or more
[agent:result]   MLflow models from the Databricks Model Registry, called served entities. A
[agent:result]   serving endpoint can have at most ten served entities. You can configure
[agent:result]   traffic settings to define how requests should be routed to your served
[agent:result]   entities behind an endpoint. Additionally, you can configure the scale of
[agent:result]   resources that should be applied to each served entity.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Usage:
[agent:result]   databricks serving-endpoints [flags]
[agent:result]   databricks serving-endpoints [command]
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Main Commands
[agent:result]   build-logs                                    Get build logs for a served model.
[agent:result]   create                                        Create a new serving endpoint.
[agent:result]   create-provisioned-throughput-endpoint        *Public Preview* Create a new PT serving endpoint.
[agent:result]   delete                                        Delete a serving endpoint.
[agent:result]   export-metrics                                Get metrics of a serving endpoint.
[agent:result]   get                                           Get a single serving endpoint.
[agent:result]   get-open-api                                  *Public Preview* Get the schema for a serving endpoint.
[agent:result]   list                                          Get all serving endpoints.
[agent:result]   logs                                          Get the latest logs for a served model.
[agent:result]   patch                                         Update tags of a serving endpoint.
[agent:result]   put                                           *Public Preview* Update rate limits of a serving endpoint.
[agent:result]   put-ai-gateway                                Update AI Gateway of a serving endpoint.
[agent:result]   query                                         Query a serving endpoint.
[agent:result]   update-config                                 Update config of a serving endpoint.
[agent:result]   update-notifications                          Update the email and webhook notification settings for an endpoint.
[agent:result]   update-provisioned-throughput-endpoint-config *Public Preview* Update config of a PT serving endpoint.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Permission Commands
[agent:result]   get-permission-levels                         Get serving endpoint permission levels.
[agent:result]   get-permissions                               Get serving endpoint permissions.
[agent:result]   set-permissions                               Set serving endpoint permissions.
